  "reason": "Evidence: config_008 (multimodal, PCA, ResNet50, concat) achieves 0.527 acc, while image-only ResNet50 (config_015) is very weak at 0.208 and RNA-only PCA (config_045) is 0.485. The modest ~4% multimodal gain over RNA-only suggests the image branch may be underperforming due to a weak encoder. Question: config_016 changes only the image encoder from ResNet50 to ImageNet ViT-L (keeping PCA, singleprofile, concat identical to config_008), cleanly isolating the effect of image representation quality. Why best next: With only 3 experiments done, the single largest uncertainty is whether the image modality can contribute more if given a stronger backbone. This single-variable comparison directly tells us whether to invest further in the image branch or focus on RNA encoder/fusion improvements, making it the highest-information experiment under budget constraints."
